<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  public/sitemap.xml -- the routes Google Search Console indexes.

  EVERY URL HERE MUST RESOLVE, or this file is worse than no file at all: a
  sitemap of 404s gets a domain flagged in Search Console rather than ignored, so
  adding a route means adding a rewrite to vercel.json AND a view to PATH_ROUTES
  in src/app.js. tests/features.mjs asserts the three lists agree, because that
  is the only thing keeping a hand-edited route from shipping a dead link.

  A fragment is deliberately absent from every entry. `/about` is a real path and
  `/#about` is a client-side state of `/` -- Google drops the fragment before
  indexing, so listing `/#about` would produce a duplicate of `/` six times over.
  See the note on PATH_ROUTES for why the clean paths exist at all.

  lastmod is the DEPLOY date for every URL rather than a per-page date, because
  the content is behind a login-free static shell and nothing here can know when
  an article changed. A wrong per-page lastmod is a signal Google is taught to
  ignore; an honest one it trusts.
-->
